      },
      "rationale": "The central task-document publisher re-enters the same kernel exclusive_file_lock on coordination_root/tasks/<repository> that run_task_doc_call holds before authoritative task_doc source read and preparation. Its call-scoped publication-active marker refuses nested publication before any write and resets in finally. The protected private transaction performs exact source CAS, canonical publication and copy refresh; failed refresh restores the pre-batch source snapshots before releasing the file lock. Other threads/processes wait, then the task_doc entry reads and prepares after rollback, so their questions stand. Independently prepared topology/retirement/linkage callers retain exact CAS and clean conflict refusal, with no retries. This is the built publication realization of the unchanged own-document/copy-set guarantee; it is not a per-key inverse or a successful nested publication.",
      "role": "propagation-persistence"
    },
